---
/* Hero.astro - Ubuntu Lynx Design System */
---

<section id="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="watermark" aria-hidden="true">FRICTION</div>

    <div class="fade-up">
      <div class="hero-label">Friction Scan Consulting · User Retention Engineering · Global B2B</div>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-up">
      <h1>Your system assumes<br/>an ideal user. Real users<br/><span style="color: var(--orange);">don't work that way.</span></h1>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-up">
      <p class="hero-summary">
        When your onboarding workflow or software interface lacks cognitive scaffolding,
        it forces users into friction, makes them feel lost, and drives them to abandon.
        I scan the invisible leaks in your platform logic to stop user attrition and
        protect your software revenue.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-up hero-ctas">
      <a href="mailto:yassergandhi.dev@gmail.com?subject=Friction%20Audit%20Request" class="btn-primary">
        [ Book a 15-Minute Friction Audit ]
      </a>
      <a href="#framework" class="btn-outline">
        See the methodology
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-up hero-tags">
      <span class="tag">Churn Diagnosis</span>
      <span class="tag">User Attrition</span>
      <span class="tag">Onboarding Leaks</span>
      <span class="tag">Data Fragmentation</span>
      <span class="tag">Lost LTV</span>
      <span class="tag">Friction Scan</span>
      <span class="tag">Product Adoption Engineering</span>
      <span class="tag">15 Years · Real Systems</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
